      },
      {
        "id": "AC2",
        "assertion": "Per the D4 sequence of docs/specs/deepen-authority-seams.spec.md (sources U2, E3): verdict application verifies the snapshot, mints the capability, runs beforeCommit, then commits. Positive: an approval records approval and a rework verdict requests rework and stages the planning-artifact transition. Negative: a snapshot that changed is refused with 'assurance snapshot changed before authority application' before any capability is minted. Bound: when onCommit throws, afterCommit still runs, the first error is rethrown and the committed transition stands. These hold for a Claude-configured and a Pi-configured coordinator. Agreed seams: tests/host-neutral-assurance-coordinator.test.ts, tests/review-revision-identity-conformance.test.ts.",
